/* =====================================================================
   062_iso27001_v13_execution.sql

   Bulk load of the ISO/IEC 27001:2022 Execution Obligation register, v1.3.

   Source     : Import Practice & Obligation Mapping v1.3 (4).xlsx, sheet 'Execution Register'
   Rows       : 3587 Execution Obligations

   Writes to:
     GRAC_New.requirement_obligation             parent row, one per sheet row
     GRAC_New.obligation_execution_spec   Execution detail
     GRAC_New.requirement_obligation_evidence    one evidence spec per Obligation
     GRAC_New.obligation_execution_evidence_link    Execution -> evidence link
     GRAC_New.obligation_requirement_release_map Practice + Release + Statement link
     GRAC_New.obligation_framework_statement_map Obligation -> Statement (056)

   Prerequisites : 026 (taxonomy schema), 027 (type master seed),
                   033 (event types), 052 (statements), 055 (obligation
                   description), 056 (obligation -> statement map),
                   058 (reset), 059 (masters), 060 (Practices).
                   060 MUST have run: every Obligation resolves its
                   Practice by Practice Name.
   Rerunnable    : yes.  An Obligation whose (Practice, Obligation Name)
                   already exists is skipped, and a partially loaded one is
                   repaired -- see "HOW AN OBLIGATION IS IDENTIFIED".
   Rollback      : 062_iso27001_v13_execution_rollback.sql

   FILE ENCODING
   -------------
   Saved as UTF-8 with BOM.  Several texts contain U+2019 (right single
   quotation mark, as in "organisation's").  Open in SSMS normally, or run
   with: sqlcmd -f 65001 -i 062_iso27001_v13_execution.sql
   All literals are N'' prefixed and embedded apostrophes are doubled.

   HOW AN OBLIGATION IS IDENTIFIED
   -------------------------------
   By the pair (Practice, Obligation Name) -- NOT by Obligation Name alone.

   requirement_obligation has no code column, so a natural key has to come
   out of the sheet.  Obligation Name on its own will not do it: 22 names
   are reused across the five registers, and six are reused inside this
   workbook's own registers.  The pair is unique -- all 12,071 rows across
   all five registers produce 12,071 distinct (Practice ID, Practice Name,
   Obligation Name) triples -- and validation step 5 re-proves it for this
   register before anything is written.

   Because the key is a pair, the MERGE below captures each inserted
   obligation_id against its staging row number rather than looking the row
   back up by name afterwards, which is what an OUTPUT-then-join-by-name
   would have to do and what a duplicated name would break.

   #key is then topped up with the obligation_ids of rows that already
   existed, so a re-run after a partial failure repairs the missing detail,
   evidence and mapping rows instead of skipping the Obligation whole.

   HOW A STATEMENT IS RESOLVED
   ---------------------------
   Not by looking the control up again.  Each Obligation inherits the
   Statement from the Practice mapping 060 already wrote:
   framework_statement_requirement_map gives the (Practice -> Statement)
   pair, and this script records that same Statement on the Obligation's
   own mapping row.  Whichever resolution mode 060 ran in, this follows it.

   The register sheets carry no control column of their own, so the
   expected statement_reference for each row was resolved from the
   Practices sheet at generation time and staged in #obl.  Validation
   step 6 checks it against the Statement inherited from 060's mapping, so
   a Practice that ended up under the wrong control stops the load rather
   than propagating into 12,071 Obligation mappings.

   OBLIGATION TYPE
   ---------------
   Every row is 'Execution'.  obligation_type_id is resolved from
   obligation_type_master by type_code -- 'Execution' -- and asserted
   before the load; the sheet's own 'Obligation Type' column is not
   trusted as the key.

   The code and the label are not always the same string.  027 seeds the
   Event Response type as type_code 'EventResponse' with type_name
   'Event Response', so a lookup written against the label finds nothing
   and the load stops on validation step 1.  This script looks up by
   'Execution' and uses 'Execution' only where a human-readable label is
   wanted -- the audit trail and the load report.

   EXECUTION DETAIL
   ----------------
     Action             -> obligation_execution_spec.[action]  (NOT NULL)
     Execution Frequency-> execution_frequency_id, resolved against
                           reference_option group 'frequency-types'
     Trigger Condition  -> trigger_condition
     Responsible Party  -> responsible_party
     Due Within         -> due_within

   FREQUENCY: 'Yearly' IS TRANSLATED TO 'Annual'
   ---------------------------------------------
   The workbook says Yearly; the master has said Annual since migration
   001.  The staged frequency_value is already translated -- see the
   INSERT #obl block, where a sheet 'Yearly' appears as N'Annual'.  Seeding
   Yearly as a second option would leave the Frequency dropdown offering
   two words for one thing.

   'One-time' has no equivalent in the master at all and is seeded by 059.
   Validation step 7 proves every staged frequency resolves before any
   Obligation is written, so an unresolved word aborts the load rather
   than silently leaving execution_frequency_id NULL on 1,188 rows.

   EVIDENCE
   --------
     Evidence Type        -> requirement_obligation_evidence.evidence_type_id,
                             resolved by name against evidence_type_master.
                             The ten names this workbook uses are seeded by
                             059; validation step 7 proves they all resolve.
     Evidence Description -> requirement_obligation_evidence.remarks
     Retention Period     -> blank on every row in this workbook, so
                             retention_requirement is left NULL.

   026 kept requirement_obligation_evidence as the single evidence store;
   the per-type link table (obligation_execution_evidence_link) records which
   taxonomy branch owns it.  Both are written here.

   MAKER-CHECKER
   -------------
   'obligations' is registered with is_maker_checker = 1, so interactive
   saves route through change_management.  This script is a controlled bulk
   load and writes directly, exactly as 052, 053 and 054 do.  An
   audit_trace row is written per inserted Obligation.

   COLUMN MAPPING WORTH KNOWING
   ----------------------------
     Obligation Name -> requirement_obligation.obligation_name
     Description     -> requirement_obligation.obligation_text  (needs 055)
     Keywords        -> requirement_obligation.keywords         (needs 023)
     load provenance -> requirement_obligation.remarks

   055 bound the Obligation Master form's Description box to obligation_text
   and stopped the save path from clobbering it.  Before 055 a description
   written here survived only until somebody opened the Obligation and
   clicked Save.  The preflight below checks for it.

   NOT SUPPLIED BY THE SHEET
   -------------------------
   retention_requirement : blank in the workbook.  Left NULL.
   evidence frequency    : left NULL on requirement_obligation_evidence.
   severity / mandatory  : not on requirement_obligation.  n/a.
   ===================================================================== */

SET NOCOUNT ON;
SET XACT_ABORT ON;
GO

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
-- Clear stale temp tables -- SEPARATE BATCH, ON PURPOSE
--
-- # temp tables live for the whole session, not the script.  If an earlier
-- run of a different revision of this file left #obl, #res or #key behind
-- with different columns, SQL Server binds the INSERT statements further
-- down against THAT table when it compiles the batch -- before the
-- CREATE TABLE below has had a chance to run -- and the load dies with
-- "Invalid column name" on a column this file plainly declares.
--
-- The GO after this block is what fixes it.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
IF OBJECT_ID('tempdb..#obl') IS NOT NULL DROP TABLE #obl;
IF OBJECT_ID('tempdb..#res') IS NOT NULL DROP TABLE #res;
IF OBJECT_ID('tempdb..#key') IS NOT NULL DROP TABLE #key;
GO

CREATE TABLE #obl(
    seq INT NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,
    practice_ref        NVARCHAR(100)  NOT NULL,
    practice_name       NVARCHAR(300)  NOT NULL,
    statement_reference NVARCHAR(100)  NOT NULL,
    obligation_name     NVARCHAR(500)  NOT NULL,
    obligation_desc     NVARCHAR(MAX)  NULL,
    keywords            NVARCHAR(MAX)  NULL,
    evidence_type       NVARCHAR(160)  NOT NULL,
    evidence_desc       NVARCHAR(MAX)  NULL,
    [action]          NVARCHAR(1000) NOT NULL,
    frequency_value   NVARCHAR(100)  NULL,
    trigger_condition NVARCHAR(500)  NULL,
    responsible_party NVARCHAR(250)  NULL,
    due_within        NVARCHAR(120)  NULL);
GO

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
-- Staged sheet rows
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
INSERT #obl(seq,practice_ref,practice_name,statement_reference,obligation_name,obligation_desc,keywords,evidence_type,evidence_desc,[action],frequency_value,trigger_condition,responsible_party,due_within) VALUES
(1,N'POL-01',N'Establish the information security policy',N'5.1',N'Consider Business, Legal and Risk Requirements',N'Perform Assess the requirements and risks that must shape the information security policy when Before the policy or a major revision is submitted for approval, led by Information Security with Legal, Compliance and Business Owners, and complete it Before approval. Frequency: When creating or revising the policy. Evidence required: Policy requirements assessment: Business, legal, contractual, risk and threat inputs considered.',N'business strategy; law; contract; risk; threat',N'Agreement',N'Evidence: Policy requirements assessment. Details: Business, legal, contractual, risk and threat inputs considered',N'Assess the requirements and risks that must shape the information security policy',N'Continuous',N'Before the policy or a major revision is submitted for approval',N'Information Security with Legal, Compliance and Business Owners',N'Before approval'),
(2,N'POL-02',N'Maintain topic-specific policies',N'5.1',N'Create Required Topic-Specific Policies',N'Perform Create or update a topic-specific policy when detailed mandatory requirements are needed when When risk, law, contract or the control framework identifies a policy need, led by Relevant Policy Owner with Information Security, and complete it Before the related process or control is put into use. Frequency: When a control area needs detailed direction. Evidence required: Approved topic-specific policy: Detailed requirements for the security area and intended users.',N'access; backup; incident; cryptography; classification; vulnerabilities; development',N'Agreement',N'Evidence: Approved topic-specific policy. Details: Detailed requirements for the security area and intended users',N'Create or update a topic-specific policy when detailed mandatory requirements are needed',N'Continuous',N'When risk, law, contract or the control framework identifies a policy need',N'Relevant Policy Owner with Information Security',N'Before the related process or control is put into use'),
(3,N'POL-03',N'Assign policy ownership and approval',N'5.1',N'Obtain Management Approval Before Publication',N'Perform Obtain approval from top management for the main policy and the appropriate authority for topic-specific policies when Before a new or changed policy is published, led by Policy Owner, and complete it Before publication. Frequency: Before publication or major change. Evidence required: Management approval record: Approval decision, approver, date, policy version and effective date.',N'management approval; publication; effective date',N'Policy',N'Evidence: Management approval record. Details: Approval decision, approver, date, policy version and effective date',N'Obtain approval from top management for the main policy and the appropriate authority for topic-specific policies',N'Continuous',N'Before a new or changed policy is published',N'Policy Owner',N'Before publication'),
(4,N'POL-04',N'Publish and communicate policies',N'5.1',N'Communicate Policies and Obtain Acknowledgement',N'Perform Communicate applicable policies and obtain acknowledgement that recipients understand and agree to comply where required when When a policy is issued or changed, or when a person joins a relevant role, led by Policy Owner with Human Resources or relevant Relationship Owner, and complete it Within the approved communication period. Frequency: On publication, update or onboarding. Evidence required: Policy communication and acknowledgement record: Recipients, policy version, communication date and acknowledgement status.',N'communication; acknowledgement; compliance; personnel',N'Policy',N'Evidence: Policy communication and acknowledgement record. Details: Recipients, policy version, communication date and acknowledgement status',N'Communicate applicable policies and obtain acknowledgement that recipients understand and agree to comply where required',N'Continuous',N'When a policy is issued or changed, or when a person joins a relevant role',N'Policy Owner with Human Resources or relevant Relationship Owner',N'Within the approved communication period'),
(5,N'POL-05',N'Review and improve policies',N'5.1',N'Use Audit and Management Review Results',N'Perform Evaluate audit and management review results and update affected policies and related documents when When an audit or management review identifies a policy improvement or inconsistency, led by Policy Owner with Information Security, and complete it By the agreed corrective-action due date. Frequency: After audit or management review. Evidence required: Policy improvement action record: Relevant findings, decisions, affected policies, actions, owners and completion evidence.',N'audit findings; management review; improvement; consistency',N'Policy',N'Evidence: Policy improvement action record. Details: Relevant findings, decisions, affected policies, actions, owners and completion evidence',N'Evaluate audit and management review results and update affected policies and related documents',N'Continuous',N'When an audit or management review identifies a policy improvement or inconsistency',N'Policy Owner with Information Security',N'By the agreed corrective-action due date'),
(6,N'ROL-01',N'Define the security role structure',N'5.2',N'Define Required Information Security Roles',N'Perform Define the roles needed to implement, operate and manage information security when Before the role structure or a material change is approved, led by Information Security Leader with Management, and complete it Before approval. Frequency: When establishing or changing the security organisation. Evidence required: Security role catalogue: Role purpose, responsibilities, authority, reporting line and required competence.',N'role definition; security management; operations; implementation',N'Register',N'Evidence: Security role catalogue. Details: Role purpose, responsibilities, authority, reporting line and required competence',N'Define the roles needed to implement, operate and manage information security',N'Continuous',N'Before the role structure or a material change is approved',N'Information Security Leader with Management',N'Before approval'),
(7,N'ROL-02',N'Allocate security responsibilities',N'5.2',N'Communicate Assigned Security Responsibilities',N'Perform Communicate the information security responsibilities and authority assigned to the role holder when When a security responsibility is assigned or changed, led by Line Manager or Role Owner, and complete it Before the responsibility becomes effective. Frequency: On assignment or change. Evidence required: Role communication record: Assigned duties, communication date and role-holder acknowledgement.',N'responsibility communication; role holder; understanding',N'Record',N'Evidence: Role communication record. Details: Assigned duties, communication date and role-holder acknowledgement',N'Communicate the information security responsibilities and authority assigned to the role holder',N'Continuous',N'When a security responsibility is assigned or changed',N'Line Manager or Role Owner',N'Before the responsibility becomes effective'),
(8,N'ROL-02',N'Allocate security responsibilities',N'5.2',N'Provide Local Security Responsibility Guidance',N'Perform Document additional responsibilities for specific sites or information processing facilities when When central role guidance does not fully address local conditions, led by Site Manager with Information Security, and complete it Before the local activity or facility becomes operational. Frequency: When local conditions require additional detail. Evidence required: Local security responsibility guidance: Site or facility-specific duties, contacts, escalation and approval.',N'site guidance; facility; local responsibility; processing facility',N'Document',N'Evidence: Local security responsibility guidance. Details: Site or facility-specific duties, contacts, escalation and approval',N'Document additional responsibilities for specific sites or information processing facilities',N'Continuous',N'When central role guidance does not fully address local conditions',N'Site Manager with Information Security',N'Before the local activity or facility becomes operational'),
(9,N'ROL-03',N'Assign risk and asset ownership',N'5.2',N'Authorise Residual Risk Acceptance',N'Perform Obtain documented acceptance of residual information security risk from the authorised risk owner when When treatment leaves residual risk requiring acceptance, led by Information Security Risk Owner, and complete it Before risk acceptance or service approval. Frequency: Before residual risk acceptance. Evidence required: Residual risk acceptance record: Risk, treatment, remaining exposure, accepting authority, decision and date.',N'residual risk; acceptance authority; approval; accountability',N'Record',N'Evidence: Residual risk acceptance record. Details: Risk, treatment, remaining exposure, accepting authority, decision and date',N'Obtain documented acceptance of residual information security risk from the authorised risk owner',N'One-time',N'When treatment leaves residual risk requiring acceptance',N'Information Security Risk Owner',N'Before risk acceptance or service approval'),
(10,N'ROL-04',N'Define authority and delegation',N'5.2',N'Control Delegation of Security Tasks',N'Perform Record the delegation while retaining accountability with the originally assigned role when When an assigned role delegates a security task, led by Accountable Security Role Holder, and complete it Before the delegate performs the task. Frequency: When a security task is delegated. Evidence required: Security task delegation record: Delegated task, delegate, accountable role, due date and expected evidence.',N'delegation; accountability; assigned task; oversight',N'Record',N'Evidence: Security task delegation record. Details: Delegated task, delegate, accountable role, due date and expected evidence',N'Record the delegation while retaining accountability with the originally assigned role',N'Continuous',N'When an assigned role delegates a security task',N'Accountable Security Role Holder',N'Before the delegate performs the task'),
