(12,N'SOD-01',N'Identify conflicting duties',N'5.3',N'Assess Processes for Conflicting Duties',N'Perform Assess whether one person can initiate, approve, execute or conceal a sensitive activity when When a new process is designed or a material process or role change occurs, led by Process Owner with Information Security, and complete it Before process approval or change implementation. Frequency: During process design and major change. Evidence required: Segregation assessment: Process steps, role assignments, identified conflicts and decisions.',N'process review; fraud; error; control bypass',N'Process',N'Evidence: Segregation assessment. Details: Process steps, role assignments, identified conflicts and decisions',N'Assess whether one person can initiate, approve, execute or conceal a sensitive activity',N'Continuous',N'When a new process is designed or a material process or role change occurs',N'Process Owner with Information Security',N'Before process approval or change implementation'),
(13,N'SOD-02',N'Separate critical activities',N'5.3',N'Separate Development, Production and Review Duties',N'Perform Assign conflicting technical and assurance activities to different authorised people when When technical, production or assurance responsibilities are assigned, led by System Owner with Line Manager and Information Security, and complete it Before access or responsibility is granted. Frequency: Before role or access assignment. Evidence required: Role assignment approval: Evidence that development, production administration and independent review duties are separated.',N'development; production; code review; assurance',N'Record',N'Evidence: Role assignment approval. Details: Evidence that development, production administration and independent review duties are separated',N'Assign conflicting technical and assurance activities to different authorised people',N'One-time',N'When technical, production or assurance responsibilities are assigned',N'System Owner with Line Manager and Information Security',N'Before access or responsibility is granted'),
(14,N'SOD-03',N'Prevent conflicting access roles',N'5.3',N'Check Conflicts Before Granting Access',N'Perform Check the requested access against incompatible role rules and resolve any conflict when When access or a role change is requested, led by Access Approver with System Owner, and complete it Before access is granted or changed. Frequency: Before access is granted or changed. Evidence required: Access conflict check: Requested roles, conflict result, decision and approval.',N'access request; conflict check; role assignment',N'Record',N'Evidence: Access conflict check. Details: Requested roles, conflict result, decision and approval',N'Check the requested access against incompatible role rules and resolve any conflict',N'One-time',N'When access or a role change is requested',N'Access Approver with System Owner',N'Before access is granted or changed'),
(15,N'SOD-04',N'Apply alternative controls',N'5.3',N'Apply Monitoring and Supervision Where Separation Is Difficult',N'Perform Implement the approved alternative controls before permitting the conflicting duties when When staffing, system design or operational limits prevent full separation, led by Process Owner with Risk Owner and Information Security, and complete it Before the exception becomes effective. Frequency: When full separation cannot be achieved. Evidence required: Alternative control implementation record: Monitoring, audit trail, review or supervision configured for the exception.',N'monitoring; audit trail; management supervision; small team',N'Configuration/Screenshot',N'Evidence: Alternative control implementation record. Details: Monitoring, audit trail, review or supervision configured for the exception',N'Implement the approved alternative controls before permitting the conflicting duties',N'Continuous',N'When staffing, system design or operational limits prevent full separation',N'Process Owner with Risk Owner and Information Security',N'Before the exception becomes effective'),
(16,N'MGT-01',N'Set management security expectations',N'5.4',N'Communicate Management Support for Security',N'Perform Communicate management support for security policies, procedures and controls when At the planned annual communication or after a major policy change, led by Executive Management and Line Managers, and complete it Within the approved communication period. Frequency: At least annually and after major policy change. Evidence required: Management communication record: Message, audience, date and security expectations communicated.',N'leadership message; policy support; role model',N'Policy',N'Evidence: Management communication record. Details: Message, audience, date and security expectations communicated',N'Communicate management support for security policies, procedures and controls',N'Annual',N'At the planned annual communication or after a major policy change',N'Executive Management and Line Managers',N'Within the approved communication period'),
(17,N'MGT-02',N'Brief personnel before access',N'5.4',N'Brief Personnel on Security Duties Before Access',N'Perform Brief the person on applicable security responsibilities and approved working methods when Before initial access to organisational information or assets, led by Line Manager with System or Information Owner, and complete it Before access is granted. Frequency: Before access is granted. Evidence required: Security responsibility briefing record: Role duties, applicable rules, briefing date and acknowledgement.',N'pre-access briefing; responsibilities; working methods',N'Record',N'Evidence: Security responsibility briefing record. Details: Role duties, applicable rules, briefing date and acknowledgement',N'Brief the person on applicable security responsibilities and approved working methods',N'One-time',N'Before initial access to organisational information or assets',N'Line Manager with System or Information Owner',N'Before access is granted'),
(18,N'MGT-03',N'Maintain awareness and competence — Management responsibilities',N'5.4',N'Complete Required Security Awareness and Training',N'Perform Complete the security awareness and role-based training assigned to the person when When a person joins, changes role or reaches the refresher due date, led by Personnel with Line Manager oversight, and complete it Within the approved learning period. Frequency: At onboarding and at the approved interval. Evidence required: Training completion record: Course, participant, completion date, result and overdue action.',N'awareness; training; skills; completion',N'Record',N'Evidence: Training completion record. Details: Course, participant, completion date, result and overdue action',N'Complete the security awareness and role-based training assigned to the person',N'Continuous',N'When a person joins, changes role or reaches the refresher due date',N'Personnel with Line Manager oversight',N'Within the approved learning period'),
(19,N'MGT-04',N'Provide security resources and time',N'5.4',N'Include Security Work in Project and Operational Plans',N'Perform Include required security activities, resources and time in the relevant plan when When a project, service or major operational change is planned, led by Project or Service Manager with Control Owners, and complete it Before plan approval. Frequency: During planning and major change. Evidence required: Project or operational plan: Security activities, effort, resources, milestones and owners.',N'security task; project time; operational plan; capacity',N'Document',N'Evidence: Project or operational plan. Details: Security activities, effort, resources, milestones and owners',N'Include required security activities, resources and time in the relevant plan',N'Continuous',N'When a project, service or major operational change is planned',N'Project or Service Manager with Control Owners',N'Before plan approval'),
(20,N'AUT-01',N'Identify and maintain authority contacts',N'5.5',N'Identify Applicable Authorities',N'Perform Identify the authorities relevant to information security, incidents and continuity when During annual review or after a significant business, location or regulatory change, led by Legal and Compliance with Information Security, and complete it Before the change takes effect or by the annual review date. Frequency: Annual and after significant change. Evidence required: Authority applicability assessment: Business locations, services, incidents and continuity needs considered.',N'authority assessment; jurisdiction; legal duty',N'Report',N'Evidence: Authority applicability assessment. Details: Business locations, services, incidents and continuity needs considered',N'Identify the authorities relevant to information security, incidents and continuity',N'Annual',N'During annual review or after a significant business, location or regulatory change',N'Legal and Compliance with Information Security',N'Before the change takes effect or by the annual review date'),
(21,N'AUT-02',N'Define authority contact responsibilities',N'5.5',N'Brief Authorised Contacts',N'Perform Brief authorised contacts on when, how and what they may communicate when When a person is assigned or the reporting process changes, led by Information Security with Legal or Compliance, and complete it Before the person performs the contact role. Frequency: On assignment or change. Evidence required: Authority-contact briefing record: Responsibilities, procedures, approval rules and acknowledgement.',N'authority communication; briefing; responsibility',N'Process',N'Evidence: Authority-contact briefing record. Details: Responsibilities, procedures, approval rules and acknowledgement',N'Brief authorised contacts on when, how and what they may communicate',N'Continuous',N'When a person is assigned or the reporting process changes',N'Information Security with Legal or Compliance',N'Before the person performs the contact role'),
(22,N'AUT-03',N'Define reporting triggers and timelines',N'5.5',N'Report Incidents Within the Required Time',N'Perform Send the approved incident report using the authority’s required method when When the assessment confirms that reporting is required, led by Authorised Authority Contact, and complete it Within the applicable reporting deadline. Frequency: When reporting is required. Evidence required: Authority notification record: Authority, information sent, sender, approval, time and receipt.',N'authority notification; deadline; incident report',N'Report',N'Evidence: Authority notification record. Details: Authority, information sent, sender, approval, time and receipt',N'Send the approved incident report using the authority’s required method',N'Continuous',N'When the assessment confirms that reporting is required',N'Authorised Authority Contact',N'Within the applicable reporting deadline'),
