(24,N'SIG-01',N'Identify relevant security groups',N'5.6',N'Assess Suitable Security Groups',N'Perform Assess which specialist groups and professional associations can support security needs when During annual review or after a significant technology, service or risk change, led by Information Security with relevant Technical Owners, and complete it By the annual review date or before the changed service begins. Frequency: Annual and after significant change. Evidence required: Security group assessment: Business, technology, sector, location and risk needs considered.',N'group assessment; sector; technology; risk',N'Report',N'Evidence: Security group assessment. Details: Business, technology, sector, location and risk needs considered',N'Assess which specialist groups and professional associations can support security needs',N'Annual',N'During annual review or after a significant technology, service or risk change',N'Information Security with relevant Technical Owners',N'By the annual review date or before the changed service begins'),
(25,N'SIG-02',N'Maintain group contacts and participation',N'5.6',N'Maintain Membership and Contact Access',N'Perform Update membership, contact and access information and complete required renewals when When contact details, owner, access or membership term changes, led by Group Liaison Owner, and complete it Before access is needed or membership expires. Frequency: On change and before renewal. Evidence required: Membership maintenance record: Current contacts, access, renewal date, owner and status.',N'membership; credentials; contact; renewal',N'Record',N'Evidence: Membership maintenance record. Details: Current contacts, access, renewal date, owner and status',N'Update membership, contact and access information and complete required renewals',N'Continuous',N'When contact details, owner, access or membership term changes',N'Group Liaison Owner',N'Before access is needed or membership expires'),
(26,N'SIG-03',N'Use security updates and specialist advice',N'5.6',N'Monitor Alerts and Advisories',N'Perform Review alerts, advisories, patches and best-practice updates received from approved groups when When new security information is received, led by Group Liaison or Security Operations, and complete it Within the risk-based review time. Frequency: As received. Evidence required: Security information intake log: Source, date, topic, relevance, recipient and action.',N'alert; advisory; patch; attack; vulnerability',N'Log',N'Evidence: Security information intake log. Details: Source, date, topic, relevance, recipient and action',N'Review alerts, advisories, patches and best-practice updates received from approved groups',N'Continuous',N'When new security information is received',N'Group Liaison or Security Operations',N'Within the risk-based review time'),
(27,N'SIG-04',N'Exchange information safely',N'5.6',N'Approve Sensitive Information Before Sharing',N'Perform Review and approve sensitive security information before sharing it with a group or member when When proposed external sharing includes non-public organisational information, led by Information Owner with Information Security, and complete it Before the information is shared. Frequency: Before external sharing. Evidence required: Information-sharing approval: Information, classification, recipient, purpose, protection and approver.',N'external sharing; sensitive information; approval',N'Record',N'Evidence: Information-sharing approval. Details: Information, classification, recipient, purpose, protection and approver',N'Review and approve sensitive security information before sharing it with a group or member',N'One-time',N'When proposed external sharing includes non-public organisational information',N'Information Owner with Information Security',N'Before the information is shared'),
(28,N'THR-01',N'Govern threat intelligence',N'5.7',N'Define Threat-Intelligence Requirements',N'Perform Define the threat information required to protect the organisation and support decisions when During annual planning or after significant business, technology or threat change, led by Threat-Intelligence Owner with Risk and Security Stakeholders, and complete it Before the collection plan is approved. Frequency: Annual and after significant change. Evidence required: Intelligence requirements record: Stakeholders, decisions supported, priority topics, scope and update need.',N'information need; stakeholder; decision; priority',N'Document',N'Evidence: Intelligence requirements record. Details: Stakeholders, decisions supported, priority topics, scope and update need',N'Define the threat information required to protect the organisation and support decisions',N'Annual',N'During annual planning or after significant business, technology or threat change',N'Threat-Intelligence Owner with Risk and Security Stakeholders',N'Before the collection plan is approved'),
(29,N'THR-02',N'Cover all intelligence levels',N'5.7',N'Produce Strategic Threat Intelligence',N'Perform Analyse high-level threat-landscape changes relevant to organisational strategy and risk when At the planned reporting cycle or when a major threat-landscape change occurs, led by Threat-Intelligence Team or Information Security, and complete it Within the approved reporting cycle. Frequency: Quarterly and on major change. Evidence required: Strategic threat-intelligence report: Changing threat landscape, attacker types, attack types, business relevance and decisions.',N'strategic; threat landscape; attacker type; attack trend',N'Report',N'Evidence: Strategic threat-intelligence report. Details: Changing threat landscape, attacker types, attack types, business relevance and decisions',N'Analyse high-level threat-landscape changes relevant to organisational strategy and risk',N'Quarterly',N'At the planned reporting cycle or when a major threat-landscape change occurs',N'Threat-Intelligence Team or Information Security',N'Within the approved reporting cycle'),
(30,N'THR-02',N'Cover all intelligence levels',N'5.7',N'Produce Tactical Threat Intelligence',N'Perform Analyse attacker methods, tools and technologies relevant to the organisation when At the planned cycle or when material tactics, tools or techniques change, led by Threat-Intelligence or Security Operations, and complete it Within the risk-based analysis period. Frequency: Monthly and as threats change. Evidence required: Tactical threat-intelligence report: Attacker methods, tools, technologies, affected controls and recommended actions.',N'tactical; attacker method; tool; technique; technology',N'Report',N'Evidence: Tactical threat-intelligence report. Details: Attacker methods, tools, technologies, affected controls and recommended actions',N'Analyse attacker methods, tools and technologies relevant to the organisation',N'Monthly',N'At the planned cycle or when material tactics, tools or techniques change',N'Threat-Intelligence or Security Operations',N'Within the risk-based analysis period'),
(31,N'THR-02',N'Cover all intelligence levels',N'5.7',N'Produce Operational Threat Intelligence',N'Perform Analyse specific attacks and technical indicators relevant to current operations when When attack information or technical indicators are received or detected, led by Security Operations or Threat-Intelligence Team, and complete it Within the risk-based operational response time. Frequency: Continuous and as attacks emerge. Evidence required: Operational threat-intelligence product: Attack details, technical indicators, affected assets, confidence and response guidance.',N'operational; specific attack; technical indicator; IOC',N'Record',N'Evidence: Operational threat-intelligence product. Details: Attack details, technical indicators, affected assets, confidence and response guidance',N'Analyse specific attacks and technical indicators relevant to current operations',N'Continuous',N'When attack information or technical indicators are received or detected',N'Security Operations or Threat-Intelligence Team',N'Within the risk-based operational response time'),
(32,N'THR-03',N'Select and manage intelligence sources',N'5.7',N'Identify Required Internal and External Sources',N'Perform Identify internal and external sources needed to meet approved intelligence requirements when When intelligence requirements are established or changed, led by Threat-Intelligence Owner, and complete it Before collection begins. Frequency: During planning and when requirements change. Evidence required: Source selection assessment: Information requirement, candidate sources, coverage, gaps and selection decision.',N'source need; internal telemetry; external provider; agency',N'Report',N'Evidence: Source selection assessment. Details: Information requirement, candidate sources, coverage, gaps and selection decision',N'Identify internal and external sources needed to meet approved intelligence requirements',N'Continuous',N'When intelligence requirements are established or changed',N'Threat-Intelligence Owner',N'Before collection begins'),
(33,N'THR-04',N'Collect and prepare threat information',N'5.7',N'Collect Information from Approved Sources',N'Perform Collect threat information from approved internal and external sources when At the planned collection time or when a source publishes relevant information, led by Threat-Intelligence or Security Operations, and complete it Within the approved collection window. Frequency: Continuous or source-defined. Evidence required: Threat-information collection log: Source, collection time, data set, result, failure and owner.',N'collection; feed; report; telemetry; advisory',N'Log',N'Evidence: Threat-information collection log. Details: Source, collection time, data set, result, failure and owner',N'Collect threat information from approved internal and external sources',N'Continuous',N'At the planned collection time or when a source publishes relevant information',N'Threat-Intelligence or Security Operations',N'Within the approved collection window'),
(34,N'THR-04',N'Collect and prepare threat information',N'5.7',N'Translate and Format Collected Information',N'Perform Translate and format collected information so it can be consistently analysed when When collected information is in an unsupported language, format or structure, led by Threat-Intelligence Analyst or approved processing system, and complete it Before analysis. Frequency: As information is collected. Evidence required: Threat-information processing record: Input, translation or format change, output, time and processing result.',N'translation; formatting; schema; preparation',N'Report',N'Evidence: Threat-information processing record. Details: Input, translation or format change, output, time and processing result',N'Translate and format collected information so it can be consistently analysed',N'One-time',N'When collected information is in an unsupported language, format or structure',N'Threat-Intelligence Analyst or approved processing system',N'Before analysis'),
(35,N'THR-04',N'Collect and prepare threat information',N'5.7',N'Corroborate Threat Information',N'Perform Compare material threat information with other reliable sources and assign confidence when Before information is used for a material decision or control change, led by Threat-Intelligence Analyst, and complete it Before publication or operational use. Frequency: Before material use where practical. Evidence required: Threat-information corroboration record: Claim or indicator, confirming sources, conflicts, confidence and decision.',N'corroboration; validation; multiple source; confidence',N'Record',N'Evidence: Threat-information corroboration record. Details: Claim or indicator, confirming sources, conflicts, confidence and decision',N'Compare material threat information with other reliable sources and assign confidence',N'One-time',N'Before information is used for a material decision or control change',N'Threat-Intelligence Analyst',N'Before publication or operational use'),
(36,N'THR-05',N'Analyse and quality-check intelligence',N'5.7',N'Analyse Organisational Relevance',N'Perform Determine how collected threat information relates to the organisation and its protection needs when When information is selected for intelligence production, led by Threat-Intelligence Analyst with relevant Asset Owners, and complete it Before intelligence is communicated. Frequency: For each intelligence product. Evidence required: Threat relevance analysis: Threat, affected assets or services, exposure, relevance decision and rationale.',N'relevance; asset; service; organisation; exposure',N'Report',N'Evidence: Threat relevance analysis. Details: Threat, affected assets or services, exposure, relevance decision and rationale',N'Determine how collected threat information relates to the organisation and its protection needs',N'Continuous',N'When information is selected for intelligence production',N'Threat-Intelligence Analyst with relevant Asset Owners',N'Before intelligence is communicated'),
(37,N'THR-05',N'Analyse and quality-check intelligence',N'5.7',N'Add Situational Context',N'Perform Add the context needed to understand when, where and how the threat is relevant when During analysis of selected threat information, led by Threat-Intelligence Analyst, and complete it Before intelligence is communicated. Frequency: For each intelligence product. Evidence required: Contextual threat analysis: Timing, location, previous experience, industry prevalence and organisational conditions.',N'context; time; location; history; prevalence',N'Report',N'Evidence: Contextual threat analysis. Details: Timing, location, previous experience, industry prevalence and organisational conditions',N'Add the context needed to understand when, where and how the threat is relevant',N'Continuous',N'During analysis of selected threat information',N'Threat-Intelligence Analyst',N'Before intelligence is communicated'),
(38,N'THR-05',N'Analyse and quality-check intelligence',N'5.7',N'Define Actionable Recommendations',N'Perform Translate intelligence into clear actions that can be taken quickly and effectively when When analysis identifies a threat relevant to the organisation, led by Threat-Intelligence Analyst with Control or Risk Owner, and complete it Within the threat-priority response period. Frequency: For each relevant intelligence product. Evidence required: Threat-intelligence action recommendation: Recommended action, priority, owner, timing, expected effect and dependencies.',N'actionable; recommendation; owner; urgency',N'Report',N'Evidence: Threat-intelligence action recommendation. Details: Recommended action, priority, owner, timing, expected effect and dependencies',N'Translate intelligence into clear actions that can be taken quickly and effectively',N'Continuous',N'When analysis identifies a threat relevant to the organisation',N'Threat-Intelligence Analyst with Control or Risk Owner',N'Within the threat-priority response period'),
(39,N'THR-06',N'Communicate threat intelligence',N'5.7',N'Communicate Intelligence to Relevant People',N'Perform Share relevant intelligence with the people able to decide or act, in an understandable format when When an intelligence product is approved or urgent information is validated, led by Threat-Intelligence Owner or Analyst, and complete it Within the threat-priority communication time. Frequency: As intelligence becomes relevant. Evidence required: Intelligence distribution record: Product, recipients, format, time, classification and acknowledgement where needed.',N'recipient; understandable format; timely sharing',N'Record',N'Evidence: Intelligence distribution record. Details: Product, recipients, format, time, classification and acknowledgement where needed',N'Share relevant intelligence with the people able to decide or act, in an understandable format',N'Continuous',N'When an intelligence product is approved or urgent information is validated',N'Threat-Intelligence Owner or Analyst',N'Within the threat-priority communication time'),
(40,N'THR-07',N'Use intelligence in security activities',N'5.7',N'Integrate Intelligence into Risk Management',N'Perform Use relevant threat intelligence in risk identification, assessment and treatment decisions when When intelligence changes understanding of a threat or during planned risk review, led by Risk Owner with Information Security, and complete it Within the risk-review or threat-priority period. Frequency: On relevant intelligence and during risk review. Evidence required: Risk-management integration record: Intelligence input, affected risk, rating change, treatment and owner.',N'risk assessment; risk register; threat scenario; treatment',N'Register',N'Evidence: Risk-management integration record. Details: Intelligence input, affected risk, rating change, treatment and owner',N'Use relevant threat intelligence in risk identification, assessment and treatment decisions',N'Continuous',N'When intelligence changes understanding of a threat or during planned risk review',N'Risk Owner with Information Security',N'Within the risk-review or threat-priority period'),
(41,N'THR-07',N'Use intelligence in security activities',N'5.7',N'Update Preventive Controls from Intelligence',N'Perform Use actionable intelligence as input to relevant preventive controls when When intelligence identifies indicators, methods or exposure requiring prevention, led by Security Operations or Control Owner, and complete it Within the threat-priority change period. Frequency: On actionable intelligence. Evidence required: Preventive control update record: Intelligence, affected control, approved change, implementation and validation.',N'firewall; anti-malware; block; preventive control',N'Record',N'Evidence: Preventive control update record. Details: Intelligence, affected control, approved change, implementation and validation',N'Use actionable intelligence as input to relevant preventive controls',N'Continuous',N'When intelligence identifies indicators, methods or exposure requiring prevention',N'Security Operations or Control Owner',N'Within the threat-priority change period'),
(42,N'THR-07',N'Use intelligence in security activities',N'5.7',N'Update Detective Controls from Intelligence',N'Perform Use actionable intelligence to update intrusion detection, monitoring or other detective controls when When intelligence provides behaviours or indicators suitable for detection, led by Security Monitoring or Detection Engineering, and complete it Within the threat-priority change period. Frequency: On actionable intelligence. Evidence required: Detective control update record: Intelligence, detection logic, implementation, test and monitoring result.',N'intrusion detection; monitoring; alert rule; indicator',N'Record',N'Evidence: Detective control update record. Details: Intelligence, detection logic, implementation, test and monitoring result',N'Use actionable intelligence to update intrusion detection, monitoring or other detective controls',N'Continuous',N'When intelligence provides behaviours or indicators suitable for detection',N'Security Monitoring or Detection Engineering',N'Within the threat-priority change period'),
(43,N'THR-07',N'Use intelligence in security activities',N'5.7',N'Use Intelligence in Security Testing',N'Perform Use relevant threat intelligence to design or update security tests and techniques when During planned security testing or when a major relevant threat emerges, led by Security Testing Team with Threat-Intelligence Analyst, and complete it Before the relevant test cycle completes. Frequency: During test planning and on major threat change. Evidence required: Threat-informed security test plan: Threat input, test scenario, scope, expected result, execution and findings.',N'test case; attack method; indicator; validation',N'Document',N'Evidence: Threat-informed security test plan. Details: Threat input, test scenario, scope, expected result, execution and findings',N'Use relevant threat intelligence to design or update security tests and techniques',N'Continuous',N'During planned security testing or when a major relevant threat emerges',N'Security Testing Team with Threat-Intelligence Analyst',N'Before the relevant test cycle completes'),
(44,N'THR-08',N'Share and improve threat intelligence',N'5.7',N'Share Threat Intelligence on a Mutual Basis',N'Perform Exchange appropriate threat intelligence with approved organisations under mutual arrangements when When useful intelligence is available or requested under the approved arrangement, led by Authorised Threat-Intelligence Liaison, and complete it Within the agreed sharing time. Frequency: As agreed and when useful. Evidence required: Threat-intelligence sharing record: Information shared or received, partner, approval, protections, date and value.',N'information exchange; partner; threat; indicator',N'Record',N'Evidence: Threat-intelligence sharing record. Details: Information shared or received, partner, approval, protections, date and value',N'Exchange appropriate threat intelligence with approved organisations under mutual arrangements',N'Continuous',N'When useful intelligence is available or requested under the approved arrangement',N'Authorised Threat-Intelligence Liaison',N'Within the agreed sharing time'),
(45,N'ISPM-01',N'Govern project security',N'5.8',N'Assign Project Security Responsibilities',N'Perform Assign and approve security responsibilities for the project when Before project work starts, led by Project Sponsor and Project Manager, and complete it Before project kickoff. Frequency: At project initiation. Evidence required: Responsibility record: Named security owners, approvers and escalation contacts.',N'security owner; roles; authority; escalation',N'Record',N'Evidence: Responsibility record. Details: Named security owners, approvers and escalation contacts',N'Assign and approve security responsibilities for the project',N'One-time',N'Before project work starts',N'Project Sponsor and Project Manager',N'Before project kickoff'),
(46,N'ISPM-02',N'Manage project security risks',N'5.8',N'Complete the Initial Security Risk Assessment',N'Perform Identify and assess information security risks when Before design, procurement or delivery decisions, led by Project Manager with Information Security, and complete it Before the first project approval. Frequency: At project initiation. Evidence required: Security risk assessment: Recorded risks, ratings, owners and planned treatments.',N'initial assessment; project risk; early review',N'Report',N'Evidence: Security risk assessment. Details: Recorded risks, ratings, owners and planned treatments',N'Identify and assess information security risks',N'One-time',N'Before design, procurement or delivery decisions',N'Project Manager with Information Security',N'Before the first project approval'),
(47,N'ISPM-03',N'Define security requirements',N'5.8',N'Document Security Requirements Early',N'Perform Document the security requirements for the project deliverable when Before design approval, led by Business Owner, Project Manager and Information Security, and complete it Before design approval. Frequency: During planning and design. Evidence required: Security requirements record: Approved security requirements with source and acceptance criteria.',N'security requirements; planning; design; compliance',N'Document',N'Evidence: Security requirements record. Details: Approved security requirements with source and acceptance criteria',N'Document the security requirements for the project deliverable',N'One-time',N'Before design approval',N'Business Owner, Project Manager and Information Security',N'Before design approval'),
(48,N'ISPM-03',N'Define security requirements',N'5.8',N'Classify Information and Set Protection Needs',N'Perform Identify project information and define confidentiality, integrity and availability needs when Before information is collected, created or shared, led by Information Owner with Project Manager, and complete it Before information use. Frequency: During planning. Evidence required: Information assessment: Information list, classification, business impact and protection needs.',N'classification; confidentiality; integrity; availability; business impact',N'Report',N'Evidence: Information assessment. Details: Information list, classification, business impact and protection needs',N'Identify project information and define confidentiality, integrity and availability needs',N'One-time',N'Before information is collected, created or shared',N'Information Owner with Project Manager',N'Before information use'),
(49,N'ISPM-04',N'Control access and user duties',N'5.8',N'Approve Access Before Granting It',N'Perform Approve and provision only the access needed for the project role when When project access is requested, led by System Owner or Information Owner, and complete it Before access is granted. Frequency: Before access is granted. Evidence required: Access approval record: Approved request showing user, role, system, access level and expiry.',N'access request; approval; least privilege; authentication',N'Record',N'Evidence: Access approval record. Details: Approved request showing user, role, system, access level and expiry',N'Approve and provision only the access needed for the project role',N'One-time',N'When project access is requested',N'System Owner or Information Owner',N'Before access is granted'),
(50,N'ISPM-04',N'Control access and user duties',N'5.8',N'Brief People on Project Security Duties',N'Perform Explain the security duties that apply to each project role when When a person joins or receives changed responsibilities, led by Project Manager or Information Security, and complete it Before access or new duties begin. Frequency: At onboarding and when duties change. Evidence required: Security briefing record: Briefing content, attendees, date and acknowledgement.',N'security duties; awareness; project team; supplier',N'Record',N'Evidence: Security briefing record. Details: Briefing content, attendees, date and acknowledgement',N'Explain the security duties that apply to each project role',N'Continuous',N'When a person joins or receives changed responsibilities',N'Project Manager or Information Security',N'Before access or new duties begin'),
(51,N'ISPM-06',N'Manage supplier security',N'5.8',N'Assess Supplier Security Before Engagement',N'Perform Assess whether the supplier can meet project security requirements when Before contract award or access approval, led by Procurement with Information Security and Project Manager, and complete it Before supplier engagement. Frequency: Before supplier selection. Evidence required: Supplier security assessment: Completed assessment, risks, conditions and approval.',N'supplier assessment; due diligence; security capability',N'Agreement',N'Evidence: Supplier security assessment. Details: Completed assessment, risks, conditions and approval',N'Assess whether the supplier can meet project security requirements',N'One-time',N'Before contract award or access approval',N'Procurement with Information Security and Project Manager',N'Before supplier engagement'),
(52,N'ISPM-07',N'Plan for incidents and continuity',N'5.8',N'Use Threat and Incident Lessons in Design',N'Perform Review likely threats and past incidents and update the project requirements when Before design approval, led by Solution Owner with Information Security, and complete it Before design approval. Frequency: During planning and design. Evidence required: Threat and incident review: Relevant threats, lessons, vulnerability limits and resulting requirements.',N'threat review; incident lessons; vulnerability; design',N'Document',N'Evidence: Threat and incident review. Details: Relevant threats, lessons, vulnerability limits and resulting requirements',N'Review likely threats and past incidents and update the project requirements',N'One-time',N'Before design approval',N'Solution Owner with Information Security',N'Before design approval'),
(53,N'ISPM-08',N'Test and approve security',N'5.8',N'Retain Project Security Closure Evidence',N'Perform Compile and store the project security evidence when When the project is ready to close, led by Project Manager, and complete it Before formal project closure. Frequency: At project closure. Evidence required: Security closure pack: Final requirements, risk register, test results, approvals and accepted risks.',N'closure evidence; approvals; test results; risk acceptance',N'Register',N'Evidence: Security closure pack. Details: Final requirements, risk register, test results, approvals and accepted risks',N'Compile and store the project security evidence',N'One-time',N'When the project is ready to close',N'Project Manager',N'Before formal project closure'),
(54,N'AST-01',N'Identify information and associated assets',N'5.9',N'Identify Organisational Information Assets',N'Perform Identify information created, received, stored, processed or shared by the organisation when When a process, service, system or information set is created or materially changed, led by Business or Information Owner with Asset Management, and complete it Before operational use. Frequency: During process, service and system creation or review. Evidence required: Information asset identification record: Information asset, business use, source, users and responsible function.',N'information asset; data; record; knowledge',N'Process',N'Evidence: Information asset identification record. Details: Information asset, business use, source, users and responsible function',N'Identify information created, received, stored, processed or shared by the organisation',N'Continuous',N'When a process, service, system or information set is created or materially changed',N'Business or Information Owner with Asset Management',N'Before operational use'),
(55,N'AST-01',N'Identify information and associated assets',N'5.9',N'Identify Other Associated Assets',N'Perform Identify assets that store, process, transmit, protect or otherwise support organisational information when When an associated asset is acquired, created, transferred or discovered, led by Relevant Asset Management Function, and complete it Before or promptly after operational use begins. Frequency: During asset acquisition, creation or discovery. Evidence required: Associated asset identification record: Asset type, relationship to information or service, location and responsible function.',N'associated asset; hardware; software; people; facility',N'Process',N'Evidence: Associated asset identification record. Details: Asset type, relationship to information or service, location and responsible function',N'Identify assets that store, process, transmit, protect or otherwise support organisational information',N'One-time',N'When an associated asset is acquired, created, transferred or discovered',N'Relevant Asset Management Function',N'Before or promptly after operational use begins'),
(56,N'AST-01',N'Identify information and associated assets',N'5.9',N'Determine Asset Information-Security Importance',N'Perform Determine the asset’s importance to information security and organisational operations when When an asset is registered or its use, information or dependency changes materially, led by Asset Owner with Business or Risk Owner, and complete it Before protection decisions are approved. Frequency: At registration and material change. Evidence required: Asset importance assessment: Security importance, business dependency, impact and assessment rationale.',N'importance; criticality; confidentiality; integrity; availability',N'Report',N'Evidence: Asset importance assessment. Details: Security importance, business dependency, impact and assessment rationale',N'Determine the asset’s importance to information security and organisational operations',N'Continuous',N'When an asset is registered or its use, information or dependency changes materially',N'Asset Owner with Business or Risk Owner',N'Before protection decisions are approved'),
(57,N'AST-02',N'Maintain suitable asset inventories',N'5.9',N'Record Asset Location Where Appropriate',N'Perform Record and update the asset location when location is relevant to security or management when When an asset is registered, moved, hosted elsewhere or its logical location changes, led by Asset Custodian or Inventory Maintainer, and complete it Within the approved inventory-update period. Frequency: At registration and location change. Evidence required: Asset location record: Physical, logical or service location and effective date.',N'asset location; site; cloud; remote; storage',N'Register',N'Evidence: Asset location record. Details: Physical, logical or service location and effective date',N'Record and update the asset location when location is relevant to security or management',N'Continuous',N'When an asset is registered, moved, hosted elsewhere or its logical location changes',N'Asset Custodian or Inventory Maintainer',N'Within the approved inventory-update period'),
(58,N'AST-03',N'Keep inventories accurate and current',N'5.9',N'Update Inventory When Assets Are Installed',N'Perform Create or update the inventory entry as part of the asset-installation process when When an asset is installed or deployed, led by Deployment or Asset Management Function, and complete it Before or at completion of installation. Frequency: On installation. Evidence required: Asset installation and inventory record: Installed asset, identifier, date, inventory entry and responsible person or system.',N'installation; deployment; registration; automatic update',N'Register',N'Evidence: Asset installation and inventory record. Details: Installed asset, identifier, date, inventory entry and responsible person or system',N'Create or update the inventory entry as part of the asset-installation process',N'Continuous',N'When an asset is installed or deployed',N'Deployment or Asset Management Function',N'Before or at completion of installation'),
(59,N'AST-03',N'Keep inventories accurate and current',N'5.9',N'Update Inventory When Assets Change',N'Perform Update relevant inventory information as part of the approved asset-change process when When asset configuration, status, owner, location, use or relationship changes, led by Change Implementer or Inventory Maintainer, and complete it By completion of the change. Frequency: On asset change. Evidence required: Asset change and inventory record: Asset, change, previous value, new value, date and inventory update.',N'configuration change; status change; inventory update',N'Configuration/Screenshot',N'Evidence: Asset change and inventory record. Details: Asset, change, previous value, new value, date and inventory update',N'Update relevant inventory information as part of the approved asset-change process',N'Continuous',N'When asset configuration, status, owner, location, use or relationship changes',N'Change Implementer or Inventory Maintainer',N'By completion of the change'),
(60,N'AST-03',N'Keep inventories accurate and current',N'5.9',N'Update Inventory When Assets Are Removed',N'Perform Remove or correctly mark the inventory entry as part of asset removal or retirement when When an asset is removed, retired, returned or transferred out, led by Asset Custodian or Disposal Process Owner, and complete it By completion of removal. Frequency: On asset removal. Evidence required: Asset removal and inventory record: Asset, removal reason, date, disposal or transfer reference and final inventory status.',N'removal; retirement; decommission; inventory status',N'Register',N'Evidence: Asset removal and inventory record. Details: Asset, removal reason, date, disposal or transfer reference and final inventory status',N'Remove or correctly mark the inventory entry as part of asset removal or retirement',N'Continuous',N'When an asset is removed, retired, returned or transferred out',N'Asset Custodian or Disposal Process Owner',N'By completion of removal'),
(61,N'AST-04',N'Set classification and inventory detail',N'5.9',N'Classify Assets According to Associated Information',N'Perform Apply an asset classification consistent with the information associated with the asset when When an asset is registered or associated information is reclassified, led by Asset Owner with Information Owner, and complete it Before operational use or promptly after reclassification. Frequency: At registration and classification change. Evidence required: Asset classification decision: Associated information, classification applied, rationale and protection impact.',N'information classification; inherited classification; protection',N'Register',N'Evidence: Asset classification decision. Details: Associated information, classification applied, rationale and protection impact',N'Apply an asset classification consistent with the information associated with the asset',N'Continuous',N'When an asset is registered or associated information is reclassified',N'Asset Owner with Information Owner',N'Before operational use or promptly after reclassification'),
(62,N'AST-04',N'Set classification and inventory detail',N'5.9',N'Manage Short-Lived Assets Appropriately',N'Perform Record or otherwise account for short-lived assets using a practical level of detail when When short-lived or rapidly changing assets are created or discovered, led by Technology Platform Owner, and complete it According to the approved dynamic-inventory method. Frequency: On creation and termination where feasible. Evidence required: Short-lived asset management record: Asset type, discovery or grouping method, life-cycle record and justified limitations.',N'ephemeral asset; short-lived VM; dynamic inventory',N'Register',N'Evidence: Short-lived asset management record. Details: Asset type, discovery or grouping method, life-cycle record and justified limitations',N'Record or otherwise account for short-lived assets using a practical level of detail',N'Continuous',N'When short-lived or rapidly changing assets are created or discovered',N'Technology Platform Owner',N'According to the approved dynamic-inventory method'),
(63,N'AST-05',N'Assign and maintain asset ownership',N'5.9',N'Assign Ownership When Assets Are Created',N'Perform Assign ownership when the asset is created when When a new information or associated asset is created, led by Creating Function or Asset Management, and complete it At creation or before operational use. Frequency: On asset creation. Evidence required: New-asset ownership record: Asset, creation date, assigned owner and assignment date.',N'creation; ownership assignment; new asset',N'Record',N'Evidence: New-asset ownership record. Details: Asset, creation date, assigned owner and assignment date',N'Assign ownership when the asset is created',N'Continuous',N'When a new information or associated asset is created',N'Creating Function or Asset Management',N'At creation or before operational use'),
(64,N'AST-05',N'Assign and maintain asset ownership',N'5.9',N'Assign Ownership When Assets Transfer In',N'Perform Assign organisational ownership when an asset is transferred to the organisation when When an asset is received, acquired or transferred into organisational control, led by Receiving Function with Asset Management, and complete it At acceptance or before use. Frequency: On transfer to the organisation. Evidence required: Transferred-asset ownership record: Asset, transfer source, receipt date, assigned owner and acceptance.',N'asset transfer; acquisition; received asset; owner',N'Record',N'Evidence: Transferred-asset ownership record. Details: Asset, transfer source, receipt date, assigned owner and acceptance',N'Assign organisational ownership when an asset is transferred to the organisation',N'Continuous',N'When an asset is received, acquired or transferred into organisational control',N'Receiving Function with Asset Management',N'At acceptance or before use'),
(65,N'AST-06',N'Manage assets through their life cycle',N'5.9',N'Securely Handle Asset Deletion and Disposal',N'Perform Ensure deleted or disposed assets are handled securely and removed or closed in the inventory when When an information or associated asset reaches deletion or disposal, led by Asset Owner with Custodian or Disposal Process Owner, and complete it By completion of deletion or disposal. Frequency: On deletion or disposal. Evidence required: Asset deletion or disposal record: Asset, protection method, deletion or disposal evidence, date and inventory update.',N'delete; disposal; secure handling; inventory removal',N'Register',N'Evidence: Asset deletion or disposal record. Details: Asset, protection method, deletion or disposal evidence, date and inventory update',N'Ensure deleted or disposed assets are handled securely and removed or closed in the inventory',N'Continuous',N'When an information or associated asset reaches deletion or disposal',N'Asset Owner with Custodian or Disposal Process Owner',N'By completion of deletion or disposal'),
(66,N'AST-08',N'Link dependencies, risks and accountability',N'5.9',N'Involve Asset Owners in Asset Risk Management',N'Perform Involve the asset owner in identifying and managing risks related to the asset when When an asset risk is identified, assessed, treated or reviewed, led by Risk Owner with Asset Owner, and complete it Before the risk decision is approved. Frequency: During risk assessment and treatment. Evidence required: Asset risk involvement record: Asset, risk, owner input, treatment decision and acceptance responsibility.',N'asset risk; owner; assessment; treatment; acceptance',N'Report',N'Evidence: Asset risk involvement record. Details: Asset, risk, owner input, treatment decision and acceptance responsibility',N'Involve the asset owner in identifying and managing risks related to the asset',N'One-time',N'When an asset risk is identified, assessed, treated or reviewed',N'Risk Owner with Asset Owner',N'Before the risk decision is approved'),
(67,N'AST-08',N'Link dependencies, risks and accountability',N'5.9',N'Support Personnel Managing Asset Information',N'Perform Provide necessary guidance and support to personnel managing information about the owner’s assets when When a custodian or other role needs support to perform asset-management duties, led by Asset Owner, and complete it Within the operational need. Frequency: As needed and when responsibilities change. Evidence required: Asset-management support record: Personnel supported, guidance, access, resources, issue and resolution.',N'custodian support; information manager; owner support',N'Record',N'Evidence: Asset-management support record. Details: Personnel supported, guidance, access, resources, issue and resolution',N'Provide necessary guidance and support to personnel managing information about the owner’s assets',N'Continuous',N'When a custodian or other role needs support to perform asset-management duties',N'Asset Owner',N'Within the operational need'),
(68,N'USE-01',N'Establish acceptable-use rules',N'5.10',N'Implement Acceptable-Use Rules and Procedures',N'Perform Implement approved acceptable-use rules and handling procedures in relevant working practices and controls when When rules or procedures are approved or materially changed, led by Asset and Process Owners with Information Security, and complete it Before the effective date. Frequency: On approval and change. Evidence required: Acceptable-use implementation record: Rules implemented, affected processes, systems, owners and effective date.',N'implementation; process; control; working practice',N'Process',N'Evidence: Acceptable-use implementation record. Details: Rules implemented, affected processes, systems, owners and effective date',N'Implement approved acceptable-use rules and handling procedures in relevant working practices and controls',N'Continuous',N'When rules or procedures are approved or materially changed',N'Asset and Process Owners with Information Security',N'Before the effective date'),
(69,N'USE-02',N'Communicate responsibilities to users',N'5.10',N'Communicate Protection and Handling Requirements',N'Perform Communicate applicable protection and handling requirements to personnel and external-party users when When a user joins, receives access or requirements change materially, led by Line Manager or Relationship Owner with Information Security, and complete it Before access or within the approved change-communication period. Frequency: On onboarding, access and material change. Evidence required: Acceptable-use communication record: Requirements communicated, audience, date, version and acknowledgement.',N'communication; handling; protection; user',N'Record',N'Evidence: Acceptable-use communication record. Details: Requirements communicated, audience, date, version and acknowledgement',N'Communicate applicable protection and handling requirements to personnel and external-party users',N'Continuous',N'When a user joins, receives access or requirements change materially',N'Line Manager or Relationship Owner with Information Security',N'Before access or within the approved change-communication period'),
(70,N'USE-04',N'Manage use through the information life cycle',N'5.10',N'Adjust Handling for Identified Risks',N'Perform Add or change handling controls where identified risks require additional protection when When risk assessment or change identifies a handling weakness or new exposure, led by Risk Owner with Information and Asset Owners, and complete it Before the risky use or within the approved treatment period. Frequency: During risk assessment and material change. Evidence required: Risk-based handling decision: Risk, affected asset, required handling change, owner and approval.',N'risk; handling control; context; exception',N'Report',N'Evidence: Risk-based handling decision. Details: Risk, affected asset, required handling change, owner and approval',N'Add or change handling controls where identified risks require additional protection',N'Continuous',N'When risk assessment or change identifies a handling weakness or new exposure',N'Risk Owner with Information and Asset Owners',N'Before the risky use or within the approved treatment period'),
(71,N'USE-05',N'Control access and authorised users',N'5.10',N'Apply Classification-Based Access Restrictions',N'Perform Apply the access restrictions required by the asset’s information classification when When access is granted or the classification changes, led by System or Asset Custodian with Access Management, and complete it Before access or promptly after reclassification. Frequency: Before access and on classification change. Evidence required: Access implementation record: User or role, asset, classification, approved restriction and implementation date.',N'access implementation; restriction; classification',N'Record',N'Evidence: Access implementation record. Details: User or role, asset, classification, approved restriction and implementation date',N'Apply the access restrictions required by the asset’s information classification',N'Continuous',N'When access is granted or the classification changes',N'System or Asset Custodian with Access Management',N'Before access or promptly after reclassification'),
